# LLM cost tracking, Gemini usage, ELK logging, and reliability — design doc (single file)

**Purpose:** Capture a high-level architecture for **per-function / per-module LLM cost**, **Gemini-style billing dimensions** (input, output, thinking), **cost-aware logging to ELK**, **retry and hard-reset policy**, **thinking-token limits**, **audio / accuracy / cost tradeoffs**, and **structured-output failure** handling.

**Audience:** Platform / backend engineers implementing observability and cost controls around LLM calls.

---

## 1. Goals (what “good” looks like)

| Goal | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Attribution** | Know **which function / module / flow** spent how much (tokens + estimated currency). |
| **Transparency** | Split cost by **input tokens**, **output tokens**, and **thinking / reasoning** tokens where the provider bills them separately. |
| **Observability** | Emit one structured log per LLM invocation (or per stage) into **ELK** for dashboards, alerts, and chargeback. |
| **Control** | Cap **thinking** (or equivalent hidden reasoning) usage so “unlimited thinking” cannot blow the budget. |
| **Resilience** | On failure: bounded **retries**, **hard reset** window, then re-send; long tail covered by **4h**-style retry horizon where applicable. |
| **Quality vs cost** | For **audio** paths: optional **second pass** (e.g. re-send or refine) for **accuracy** (silences, tones, sentiment) with explicit **cost tradeoff**. |
| **Correctness** | **Structured output**: define **parser** and **failure** when schema validation fails — do not silently treat garbage as success. |

