## 3. Cost model — “function / code modules cost (based on cost)”

### 3.1 Dimensions to record (per invocation)

| Field (example) | Meaning |
|-----------------|--------|
| `service` / `deployment` | Owning service name. |
| `module` | Python module or package (e.g. `voice.sentiment`). |
| `function` | Callable name (e.g. `transcribe_and_analyze`). |
| `flow_id` / `trace_id` | Correlate multi-step pipelines (e.g. same audio twice). |
| `model_id` | e.g. `gemini-2.x-flash`. |
| `input_tokens` | Billable prompt tokens (incl. system + user + tool definitions as billed). |
| `output_tokens` | Generated completion tokens. |
| `thinking_tokens` | If API exposes **thinking / reasoning** usage separately (Gemini family may surface distinct usage categories — **confirm against current API docs**). |
| `audio_seconds` / `audio_bytes` | If audio is sent as input (for unit economics). |
| `invocation_count` | Same logical request split into N API calls (e.g. “send audio twice”). |
| `estimated_cost_usd` | `f(input, output, thinking, model_rate_card)` — see §3.3. |
| `latency_ms` | Wall time (separate from token cost; useful for SLOs). |

### 3.2 Why “module + function”

Chargeback and optimization need **stable labels** from code, not only “model X”. Enforce decorators or context managers so every LLM path sets `module` + `function` (and optional `feature` tag).

### 3.3 Rate card (implementation note)

- Maintain a **versioned rate table** (YAML/JSON or DB): per `model_id`, price per 1M input / output / thinking (if separately priced).
- **Recompute** `estimated_cost_usd` at log time from token counts + table version (`rate_card_version` in log) so historical logs stay interpretable after price changes.
- **Official pricing** changes often — link to provider docs in runbooks; do not hardcode only in code without version.

